        "text": "Transcribe this audio/video in full. Then structure your entire response as ONLY valid JSON (no markdown, no commentary) matching exactly this schema: {\"transcript\": string (the full transcript broken into paragraphs, each paragraph prefixed with an approximate timestamp in [MM:SS] format), \"thesis_points\": array of 3-6 strings (the core arguments/ideas of the episode), \"notable_quotes\": array of objects {\"timestamp\": \"[MM:SS]\", \"quote\": string} for the 5-8 most quotable, punchy moments suitable for short-form video clips}.",
        "inputType": "binary",
        "simplify": false,
        "options": {
          "maxOutputTokens": 8192
        }
      },
      "id": "cd0c4d6c-30e1-4e15-8bcc-f9531716aa9f",
      "name": "Gemini: Transcribe & Extract Thesis",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.googleGemini",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        -1184,
        224
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForEachItem",
        "jsCode": "const t = $input.item.json;\nlet raw = '';\ntry {\n  raw = t.candidates[0].content.parts[0].text;\n} catch (e) {\n  raw = t.text || '';\n}\nconst cleaned = raw.replace(/```json|```/g, '').trim();\nlet parsed;\ntry {\n  parsed = JSON.parse(cleaned);\n} catch (e) {\n  parsed = { transcript: raw, thesis_points: [], notable_quotes: [] };\n}\n\nreturn {\n  json: {\n    source_file_id: t.source_file_id,\n    episode_title: t.episode_title,\n    source_url: t.source_url,\n    transcript: parsed.transcript || '',\n    thesis_points: parsed.thesis_points || [],\n    notable_quotes: parsed.notable_quotes || []\n  }\n};"
      },
      "id": "3d16ec20-3a49-4e74-ab45-5a3a62131a66",
      "name": "Code: Parse Transcript & Thesis",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        -960,
        224
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "modelId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "id",
          "value": "models/gemini-2.5-flash"
        },
        "messages": {
          "values": [
            {
              "content": "=You are a ghostwriter for a founder's LinkedIn presence. Using the thesis points and transcript below, write a LinkedIn essay repurposing this episode.\n\nConstraints: 1300-2600 characters total, a strong 1-2 line hook as the very first line, short punchy paragraphs (1-3 sentences) separated by blank lines, no hashtags, at most 1-2 emoji, end with a single thought-provoking question to drive comments. Respond with ONLY the essay text — no preamble, no markdown, no commentary.\n\nThesis points:\n{{ $json.thesis_points.map(p => '- ' + p).join('\\n') }}\n\nFull transcript:\n{{ $json.transcript }}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "simplify": false,
        "builtInTools": {},
        "options": {
          "maxOutputTokens": 2048
        }
      },
      "id": "7af6f0cb-eeb7-4048-87b7-540fda1e8878",
      "name": "Gemini: Draft LinkedIn Essay",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.googleGemini",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        -736,
        128
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForEachItem",
        "jsCode": "const t = $input.item.json;\nlet raw = '';\ntry {\n  raw = t.candidates[0].content.parts[0].text;\n} catch (e) {\n  raw = t.text || '';\n}\n\nreturn {\n  json: {\n    ...t,\n    linkedin_essay: raw.trim()\n  }\n};"
      },
      "id": "56c6acbf-eec8-44b2-87cf-57200366b409",
      "name": "Code: Parse LinkedIn Essay",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        -384,
        128
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "combine",
        "combineBy": "combineByPosition",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "c07703cf-6cdf-4c6f-bc01-324d451d8c22",
      "name": "Merge Content Drafts",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.merge",
      "typeVersion": 3,
      "position": [
        -160,
        224
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "modelId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "id",
          "value": "models/gemini-2.5-flash"
        },
        "messages": {
          "values": [
            {
              "content": "=You are a social ghostwriter. Using the thesis points and transcript below, write a step-by-step breakdown thread for X/Twitter repurposing this episode.\n\nConstraints: 6-10 posts, each post 220-275 characters, post 1 is a strong hook, each subsequent post unpacks ONE step/idea with a number prefix like '2/', the last post is a soft call-to-action recapping the core thesis. Respond with ONLY valid JSON (no markdown, no commentary): an array of strings, one per post, e.g. [\"1/ ...\", \"2/ ...\"].\n\nThesis points:\n{{ $json.thesis_points.map(p => '- ' + p).join('\\n') }}\n\nFull transcript:\n{{ $json.transcript }}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "simplify": false,
        "builtInTools": {},
        "options": {
          "maxOutputTokens": 2048
        }
      },
      "id": "c6d8db49-7d8b-4476-b530-ddf0b3c060a1",
      "name": "Gemini: Draft Step-by-Step Thread",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.googleGemini",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        -736,
        320
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForEachItem",
        "jsCode": "const t = $input.item.json;\nlet raw = '';\ntry {\n  raw = t.candidates[0].content.parts[0].text;\n} catch (e) {\n  raw = t.text || '';\n}\nconst cleaned = raw.replace(/```json|```/g, '').trim();\nlet posts;\ntry {\n  posts = JSON.parse(cleaned);\n  if (!Array.isArray(posts)) posts = [String(posts)];\n} catch (e) {\n  posts = raw.split(/\\n+/).filter(Boolean);\n}\n\nreturn {\n  json: {\n    ...t,\n    twitter_thread: posts.join('\\n\\n')\n  }\n};"
      },
      "id": "d13f6a57-b868-46e6-b219-c2c687b8767e",
      "name": "Code: Parse Thread",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        -384,
        320
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForEachItem",
        "jsCode": "const left = $input.item.json;\nconst thread = $('Code: Parse Thread').item.json;\n\nconst quotes = (left.notable_quotes || []).map(q => `${q.timestamp} \"${q.quote}\"`).join('\\n');\n\nreturn {\n  json: {\n    episode_title: left.episode_title,\n    source_url: left.source_url,\n    transcript: left.transcript,\n    thesis_points: (left.thesis_points || []).map(p => `- ${p}`).join('\\n'),\n    linkedin_essay: left.linkedin_essay,\n    twitter_thread: thread.twitter_thread,\n    quote_timestamps: quotes\n  }\n};"
      },
